title: The Central Committee
subtitle: Rákosi comes to Berlin to settle accounts with Levi.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1921 and month = 2 and e21_cc_done = 0 and e21_levi_leads = 1 and levi_in_party = 1 and congress = 0 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 10
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_cc_done = 1;
Q.comintern_rep = 'Mátyás Rákosi';
// the year so far decides how the committee leans before anyone speaks
var p = 35;
p += 3 * ((Q.history_luxemburgist || 0) - (Q.history_offensive || 0));
p += (Q.independence - 50) / 2;
p += (Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction - Q.offensive_satisfaction) / 4;
if (Q.e21_livorno == 1) { p += 10; }
if (Q.e21_livorno == 3) { p -= 10; }
if (Q.open_letter == 1) { p += 5; }
if (Q.luxemburg_alive == 1) { p += 25; }
p += (Q.ecci_radek - 50) / 5;
Q.e21_cc_win_chance = Math.round(Math.max(10, Math.min(85, p)));
Q.e21_cc_odds = (Q.e21_cc_win_chance < 30) ? 1 : ((Q.e21_cc_win_chance < 55) ? 2 : 3);
Q.e21_cc_tilt = (Q.e21_cc_win_chance - 45) / 100;
!}

= The Central Committee

From 22 to 24 February the Central Committee meets in Berlin. Rákosi has come straight from Livorno with a resolution approving the Italian split, and everyone in the room understands that it is a vote on Levi. Levi has said that if it passes he will resign the chair, and Zetkin, Däumig, Adolph Hoffmann and Otto Brass will resign with him.

[? if luxemburg_alive = 1 : Rosa Luxemburg will speak before the vote. ?][? if luxemburg_alive = 0 : Thalheimer, Frölich and the Berlin members will speak for Rákosi. ?] [? if e21_cc_odds = 1 : Levi has counted the committee and does not like the count. ?][? if e21_cc_odds = 2 : Levi has counted the committee, and it is close. ?][? if e21_cc_odds = 3 : Levi has counted the committee, and thinks he has the votes. ?]

Heinrich Brandler has a compromise in his pocket: Livorno approved in principle, Levi kept in the chair.

- @fight: Fight Rákosi's resolution.
- @compromise: Ask Brandler to table his compromise.
- @resign: Let the resolution pass, and let Levi go.
- @rakosi: Vote with Rákosi.

@fight
subtitle: If we win, Levi stays and Moscow has been defied. If we lose, he goes.
on-arrival: {!
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 3;
Q.e21_cc_mode = 1;
RG.congressStart({
    id: 'cc21',
    name: 'The Central Committee',
    stake: 'Rákosi\'s resolution on Livorno, and Levi\'s chair',
    sessions: 2,
    positions: ['luxemburgist', 'offensive'],
    backing: 'luxemburgist',
    kind: 'motion',
    mandates: 'zentrale',
    delegates: 51,
    ownClose: true
});
// Thalheimer and much of the Right side with Rákosi against Levi
RG.congress.swayTo('offensive', 0.07);
if (Q.e21_cc_tilt > 0) { RG.congress.sway(Q.e21_cc_tilt * 0.5); } else { RG.congress.lose(-Q.e21_cc_tilt * 0.6); }
RG.congress.bitter(3);
!}

Levi spends the evening before the session with a list of the fifty-one members of the committee and a pencil. By midnight there are ticks, crosses and too many question marks.

@compromise
subtitle: Levi stays if Brandler's motion carries, with the Right at his elbow. Neither Levi nor Rákosi will thank us.
on-arrival: {!
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
Q.e21_cc_mode = 2;
RG.congressStart({
    id: 'cc21',
    name: 'The Central Committee',
    stake: 'Brandler\'s compromise on Livorno, and Levi\'s chair',
    sessions: 2,
    positions: ['unionist', 'offensive'],
    backing: 'unionist',
    kind: 'motion',
    mandates: 'zentrale',
    delegates: 51,
    ownClose: true
});
if (Q.e21_cc_tilt > 0) { RG.congress.sway(Q.e21_cc_tilt * 0.5); } else { RG.congress.lose(-Q.e21_cc_tilt * 0.4); }
!}

Brandler tables his resolution. Levi withdraws his own and tells his friends to vote for Brandler's. Rákosi says that a compromise with centrism is centrism.

@resign
subtitle: What happened. Brandler and Stoecker take the chair, and the theory of the offensive comes in with them.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_resigned = 1;
Q.e21_levi_leads = 0;
Q.e21_lux_leads = 0;
Q.leading_faction = 'offensive';
Q.junior_faction = 'unionist';
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 8;
RG.setRole('levi', 'Reichstag deputy');
RG.setRole('brandler', 'Chairman of the Zentrale');
RG.comply(100);
RG.news('Levi and Zetkin resign from the Zentrale', 3);
RG.ledger('Paul Levi resigned the chair after the Central Committee approved Livorno.', 'e21_levi_resigned');
!}

Rákosi's resolution passes, 28 votes to 23. Levi, Zetkin, Däumig, Hoffmann and Brass resign from the Zentrale the same evening. They mean it as a warning, and Rákosi takes it as a victory. Heinrich Brandler and Walter Stoecker take the chair, with Thalheimer and Paul Frölich at their side.

@rakosi
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Levi goes, and Ruth Fischer's people get a voice in the new Zentrale. Zinoviev will be grateful.
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids taking orders from Moscow.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
}
Q.e21_levi_resigned = 1;
Q.e21_levi_leads = 0;
Q.e21_lux_leads = 0;
Q.leading_faction = 'offensive';
Q.junior_faction = 'unionist';
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 15;
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
RG.setRole('levi', 'Reichstag deputy');
RG.setRole('brandler', 'Chairman of the Zentrale');
RG.setRole('fischer', 'Berlin organiser; member of the Zentrale');
RG.comply(100);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 10);
RG.news('The Zentrale backs Rákosi: Levi and his friends resign', 3);
RG.ledger('The Zentrale itself turned on Levi in February 1921.', 'e21_levi_resigned');
!}

The resolution passes by a wide margin, with the Zentrale's own votes. Levi and his friends resign. Brandler and Stoecker take the chair, and Ruth Fischer's Berlin members are given seats beside them.
